IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 9 (Investigations), ss 228 to 231: the limit of the Part, its words, the Minister's power to declare a company, and the inspectors for a declared company.
-- Every function of Part 9 begins with its section label `s 228` to `s 246`, so that a reference "in Part 9" (the keel's s 4(8)) is recognisable by the label; `s 228 the provision is in Part 9` states it.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. The Minister, the inspectors and the Court appear only as what their acts mean to the person.
-- Winding up has moved to the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018, which is not a source: its outcomes enter as inputs named for the fact.
-- Marks in the comments: "FALSE-kind" and "NOTHING-kind" say why a branch answers JUST FALSE or NOTHING; "fork F-Kn" points at the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `The nouns of Part 9`

-- The parties of the regulative rules of Part 9. The core's Party has no inspector (NEEDS-CORE.md: Inspector).
DECLARE `s 231 party` IS ONE OF
    `s 231 the Minister`
    `s 231 an inspector appointed under Part 9`
    `s 231 an officer or agent of a corporation` HAS `the name of the officer or agent` IS A STRING
    `s 231 a person` HAS `the name of the person` IS A STRING
    `s 231 a company` HAS `the name of the company` IS A STRING
    `s 231 a foreign company` HAS `the name of the foreign company` IS A STRING

-- The acts of the regulative rules of Part 9 (all modules of Part 9 use this type).
DECLARE `s 231 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 231(1) appoint one or more inspectors to investigate the affairs of the declared company`
    `s 233(1) report to the Minister the inspector's opinion on the affairs investigated, with the facts on which it is based`
    `s 233(1) forward a copy of the report to the registered office of the company`
    `s 233(1A) give a copy of the report to a person whose affairs it relates to in a material extent`
    `s 233(1C) give a copy of the report to a person when legal proceedings might be unduly prejudiced`
    `s 233(2) publish the report when the Attorney-General has certified that publication would be prejudicial to the administration of justice`
    `s 233(3) institute a prosecution`
    `s 233(3) give the Minister all assistance in connection with the prosecution that the person is reasonably able to give`
    `s 236(1) report on the affairs of the related corporation`
    `s 236(2) produce to the inspector all books and documents in the person's custody or power and give all assistance reasonably able`
    `s 236(4)(c) permit the corporation to have access to the books and documents taken possession of`
    `s 237(1) pay the expenses of and incidental to the investigation`
    `s 237(2)(a) make good the deficiency up to the amount of the security`
    `s 241(2) carry on business or establish or keep a place of business in Singapore`
    `s 242(1) destroy, conceal or alter a book, document or record of or relating to a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9`
    `s 242(1) send out of Singapore a book, document, record or property of a declared company with intent to defeat the purposes of Part 9`
    `s 243(3) appoint an inspector to conduct the investigation`
    `s 244(3) give the Minister information required under section 244`
    `s 244(3) make to the Minister a statement the person knows to be false in a material particular, or recklessly makes a statement false in a material particular`
    `s 245(3) exercise or purport to exercise a right to dispose of shares, or a right to be issued with shares, knowing they are subject to the restrictions`
    `s 245(3) vote in respect of shares subject to the restrictions, or appoint a proxy to vote`
    `s 245(3) notify the holders entitled to vote of the restrictions`
    `s 245(4) issue shares in contravention of the restrictions`
    `s 240(1) commence or proceed with an action or proceeding in a Court without the consent of the Minister`

§ `Section 228: the limit of Part 9`

-- src:21892 | PART 9
-- src:21894 | INVESTIGATIONS
-- src:21896 | Application of this Part
-- src:21898 | 228. This Part does not authorise any investigation into the
-- src:21899 | insurance business of a company or into the business of a banking
-- src:21900 | corporation, unless specifically provided for in this Part.
@ref Part 9 and s 228 (src:21892-21900)
GIVEN `the number of the section` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 228 the provision is in Part 9` MEANS
    `the number of the section` AT LEAST 228 AND `the number of the section` AT MOST 246     -- Part 9 runs from section 228 to section 246 in this text

@ref s 228 (src:21898-21900)
GIVEN `the investigation is into the insurance business of a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the investigation is into the business of a banking corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `Part 9 specifically provides for the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 228 Part 9 is barred from authorising the investigation` MEANS
    IF (`the investigation is into the insurance business of a company` OR `the investigation is into the business of a banking corporation`)
    THEN (IF `Part 9 specifically provides for the investigation`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is "unless specifically provided for in this Part"; an "unless" met (fork F-K17)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- "This Part does not authorise any investigation into the insurance business of a company or into the business of a banking corporation"
    ELSE NOTHING            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section bars an investigation into the insurance business of a company or the business of a banking corporation; it says nothing of any other investigation

§ `Section 229: words used in Part 9`

-- src:21904 | 229. In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears —
@ref s 229 (opening words) (src:21904-21904)
GIVEN `the word is one that section 229 defines` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the word is used` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229 the definition governs the word where it is used in Part 9` MEANS
    IF NOT `the word is one that section 229 defines`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the opening words speak of the defined terms only
    ELSE (IF `a contrary intention appears in the provision where the word is used`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In this Part, unless the contrary intention appears"
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:21906 | “company” includes a foreign company which is a declared
-- src:21907 | company;
@ref s 229 "company" (src:21906-21907)
GIVEN `the body is a foreign company which is a declared company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229 "company" the body is within the word company` MEANS
    IF `the body is a foreign company which is a declared company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“company” includes a foreign company which is a declared company" leaves the word open

-- src:21909 | “declared company” means a company or foreign company
-- src:21910 | which the Minister has by order declared to be a company to
-- src:21911 | which this Part applies;
@ref s 229 "declared company" (src:21909-21911)
GIVEN `the body is a company or foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has by order declared the body to be a company to which Part 9 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229 "declared company" the body is a declared company` MEANS
    IF `the body is a company or foreign company` AND `the Minister has by order declared the body to be a company to which Part 9 applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“declared company” means a company or foreign company which the Minister has by order declared to be a company to which this Part applies"

-- src:21916 | “officer or agent”, in relation to a corporation, includes —
-- src:21918 | (a) a director, banker, solicitor or auditor of the
-- src:21919 | corporation;
-- src:21921 | (b) a person who at any time —
-- src:21923 | (i) has been a person referred to in paragraph (a);
-- src:21924 | or
-- src:21926 | (ii) has been otherwise employed or appointed by
-- src:21927 | the corporation;
-- src:21929 | (c) a person who —
-- src:21931 | (i) has in the person’s possession any property of
-- src:21932 | the corporation;
-- src:21934 | (ii) is indebted to the corporation; or
-- src:21936 | (iii) is capable of giving information concerning the
-- src:21937 | promotion, formation, trading, dealings, affairs
-- src:21938 | or property of the corporation; and
-- src:21940 | (d) where there are reasonable grounds for suspecting or
-- src:21941 | believing that a person is a person mentioned in
-- src:21942 | paragraph (c) — that person.
@ref s 229 "officer or agent" (src:21916-21942)
GIVEN `the person is a director, banker, solicitor or auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has at any time been a director, banker, solicitor or auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has at any time been otherwise employed or appointed by the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has in the person's possession any property of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is indebted to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is capable of giving information concerning the promotion, formation, trading, dealings, affairs or property of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting or believing that the person is a person mentioned in paragraph (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 229 "officer or agent" the person is an officer or agent of the corporation` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a director, banker, solicitor or auditor of the corporation`                                                                        -- (a)
       OR `the person has at any time been a director, banker, solicitor or auditor of the corporation`                                                      -- (b)(i)
       OR `the person has at any time been otherwise employed or appointed by the corporation`                                                               -- (b)(ii)
       OR `the person has in the person's possession any property of the corporation`                                                                        -- (c)(i)
       OR `the person is indebted to the corporation`                                                                                                        -- (c)(ii)
       OR `the person is capable of giving information concerning the promotion, formation, trading, dealings, affairs or property of the corporation`      -- (c)(iii)
       OR `there are reasonable grounds for suspecting or believing that the person is a person mentioned in paragraph (c)`                                  -- (d)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“officer or agent”, in relation to a corporation, includes —" leaves the term open

§ `Section 230: the Minister's power to declare a company`

-- src:21946 | 230. The Minister may by order declare that a company or foreign
-- src:21947 | company is a company to which this Part applies if the Minister is
-- src:21948 | satisfied —
-- src:21950 | (a) that a prima facie case has been established that, for the
-- src:21951 | protection of the public or the shareholders or creditors of
-- src:21952 | the company or foreign company, it is desirable that the
-- src:21953 | affairs of the company or foreign company should be
-- src:21954 | investigated under this Part;
-- src:21956 | (b) that it is in the public interest that allegations of fraud,
-- src:21957 | misfeasance or other misconduct by persons who are or
-- src:21958 | have been concerned with the formation or management of
-- src:21959 | the company or foreign company should be investigated
-- src:21960 | under this Part;
-- src:21965 | (c) that for any other reason it is in the public interest that the
-- src:21966 | affairs of the company or foreign company should be
-- src:21967 | investigated under this Part; or
-- src:21969 | (d) in the case of a foreign company, that the appropriate
-- src:21970 | authority of another country has requested that a
-- src:21971 | declaration be made pursuant to this section in respect of
-- src:21972 | the company.
@ref s 230 (src:21946-21972)
GIVEN `the Minister is satisfied that a prima facie case has been established that, for the protection of the public or the shareholders or creditors of the body, it is desirable that its affairs should be investigated under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest that allegations of fraud, misfeasance or other misconduct by persons who are or have been concerned with the formation or management of the body should be investigated under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that for any other reason it is in the public interest that the affairs of the body should be investigated under Part 9` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body is a foreign company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister is satisfied that the appropriate authority of another country has requested that a declaration be made in respect of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 230 the Minister may by order declare the body to be a company to which Part 9 applies` MEANS
    IF    `the Minister is satisfied that a prima facie case has been established that, for the protection of the public or the shareholders or creditors of the body, it is desirable that its affairs should be investigated under Part 9`   -- (a)
       OR `the Minister is satisfied that it is in the public interest that allegations of fraud, misfeasance or other misconduct by persons who are or have been concerned with the formation or management of the body should be investigated under Part 9`   -- (b)
       OR `the Minister is satisfied that for any other reason it is in the public interest that the affairs of the body should be investigated under Part 9`   -- (c)
       OR (`the body is a foreign company` AND `the Minister is satisfied that the appropriate authority of another country has requested that a declaration be made in respect of the company`)   -- (d) "in the case of a foreign company"
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Minister may by order declare ... if the Minister is satisfied" of a listed ground; a "may" with an "if" (not "only if") gate: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-K18

§ `Section 231: inspectors for a declared company, and the expenses`

-- src:21976 | 231.—(1) Where a company or foreign company has been declared
-- src:21977 | to be a company to which this Part applies, the Minister must appoint
-- src:21978 | one or more inspectors to investigate the affairs of that company, and
-- src:21979 | to report his or her opinion thereon to the Minister.
@ref s 231(1) (src:21976-21979)
GIVEN `the company or foreign company has been declared to be a company to which Part 9 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(1) the Minister must appoint one or more inspectors to investigate the affairs of the company` MEANS
    IF `the company or foreign company has been declared to be a company to which Part 9 applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the duty arises "Where a company or foreign company has been declared"; a "where" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

-- The Minister's duty as a regulative rule: no time limit and no stated consequence, so no trace can show it breached (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 231(1) (src:21976-21979)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 231 party` `s 231 act`
`s 231(1) the Minister must appoint inspectors for a declared company` MEANS
    PARTY `s 231 the Minister`
    MUST `s 231(1) appoint one or more inspectors to investigate the affairs of the declared company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 231(1) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:21981 | (2) An inspector appointed under subsection (1) may, at any time in
-- src:21982 | the course of the inspector’s investigation, without the necessity of
-- src:21983 | making an interim report, inform the Minister of matters coming to
-- src:21984 | the inspector’s knowledge as a result of the investigation which tend
-- src:21985 | to show that an offence has been committed; and the Minister may
-- src:21986 | thereafter take such steps as the Minister may consider fit.
@ref s 231(2) (src:21981-21986)
GIVEN `the person is an inspector appointed under section 231(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matters came to the inspector's knowledge as a result of the investigation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matters tend to show that an offence has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(2) the inspector may inform the Minister of the matters without making an interim report` MEANS
    IF `the person is an inspector appointed under section 231(1)` AND `the matters came to the inspector's knowledge as a result of the investigation` AND `the matters tend to show that an offence has been committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is stated for "an inspector appointed under subsection (1)" and for "matters coming to the inspector's knowledge as a result of the investigation which tend to show that an offence has been committed"; the subsection says nothing of any other

@ref s 231(2) (src:21981-21986)
GIVEN `the Minister has been informed under subsection (2) of matters tending to show that an offence has been committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(2) the Minister may take such steps as the Minister considers fit` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has been informed under subsection (2) of matters tending to show that an offence has been committed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the Minister "may thereafter take such steps"; a "may" gated by "thereafter", which counts as "when" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, items (b) and (c); fork F-K7)

-- src:21988 | (3) The expenses of and incidental to an investigation of a declared
-- src:21989 | company must be defrayed in the first instance out of moneys
-- src:21990 | provided by Parliament.
@ref s 231(3) (src:21988-21990)
GIVEN `the expenses are expenses of and incidental to an investigation of a declared company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(3) the expenses are defrayed in the first instance out of moneys provided by Parliament` MEANS
    IF `the expenses are expenses of and incidental to an investigation of a declared company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "the expenses of and incidental to an investigation of a declared company"

-- src:21992 | (4) Where the Minister is of the opinion that the whole or any part
-- src:21993 | of the expenses of and incidental to the investigation should be paid
-- src:21994 | by the company or by any person who is convicted on a prosecution
-- src:21995 | brought under section 233(3) or who is ordered to pay damages or
-- src:21996 | restore property in proceedings under section 233(4) the Minister
-- src:21997 | may by notification in the Gazette direct that the expenses be so paid.
@ref s 231(4) (src:21992-21997)
GIVEN `the Minister is of the opinion that the whole or part of the expenses should be paid by the company or by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payer is the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payer has been convicted on a prosecution brought under section 233(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payer has been ordered to pay damages or restore property in proceedings under section 233(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(4) the Minister may by notification in the Gazette direct that the expenses be paid by the payer` MEANS
    IF    `the Minister is of the opinion that the whole or part of the expenses should be paid by the company or by the person`
       AND (`the payer is the company` OR `the payer has been convicted on a prosecution brought under section 233(3)` OR `the payer has been ordered to pay damages or restore property in proceedings under section 233(4)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection begins "Where the Minister is of the opinion that ..."; a "may" gated by "where" (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-K7)

-- src:21999 | (5) A notification under subsection (4) may specify the time or
-- src:22000 | times and the manner in which the payment of the expenses must be
-- src:22001 | made.
@ref s 231(5) (src:21999-22001)
GIVEN `the notification is a notification under subsection (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(5) the notification may specify the time or times and the manner in which the payment of the expenses must be made` MEANS
    IF `the notification is a notification under subsection (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "A notification under subsection (4)"

-- src:22003 | (6) Where a notification has been published by the Minister under
-- src:22004 | subsection (5), the persons named in the notification to the extent
-- src:22005 | therein specified shall be liable to reimburse the Minister in respect of
-- src:22006 | such expenses.
@ref s 231(6) (src:22003-22006)
GIVEN `a notification has been published by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is named in the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(6) the person named in the notification is liable to reimburse the Minister in respect of the expenses to the extent specified` MEANS
    IF `a notification has been published by the Minister` AND `the person is named in the notification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the liability arises "Where a notification has been published" and for "the persons named in the notification"; a "where" unmet (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b); fork F-K19: the subsection says "under subsection (5)")

-- src:22011 | (7) Action to recover any such expenses may be taken in the name
-- src:22012 | of the Government in any court of competent jurisdiction.
@ref s 231(7) (src:22011-22012)
GIVEN `the expenses are expenses a person is liable to reimburse under subsection (6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(7) action to recover the expenses may be taken in the name of the Government in any court of competent jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the expenses are expenses a person is liable to reimburse under subsection (6)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "any such expenses", those of subsection (6)

-- src:22014 | (8) Where a notification under subsection (4) has been published
-- src:22015 | for the payment of the whole or part of the expenses by a company
-- src:22016 | and the company is in liquidation or subsequently goes into
-- src:22017 | liquidation the expenses so ordered to be paid by the company are
-- src:22018 | deemed to be part of the costs and expenses of the winding up for the
-- src:22019 | purposes of section 203(1)(a) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:22020 | Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 231(8) (src:22014-22020)
GIVEN `a notification under subsection (4) has been published for the payment of the whole or part of the expenses by a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is in liquidation or subsequently goes into liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(8) the expenses ordered to be paid by the company are part of the costs and expenses of the winding up for the purposes of section 203(1)(a) of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018` MEANS
    IF `a notification under subsection (4) has been published for the payment of the whole or part of the expenses by a company` AND `the company is in liquidation or subsequently goes into liquidation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the deeming applies "Where a notification under subsection (4) has been published ... and the company is in liquidation or subsequently goes into liquidation"; a "where" unmet (periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

-- src:22024 | (9) The report of the inspector may if the inspector thinks fit, and
-- src:22025 | must, if the Minister so directs, include a recommendation as to the
-- src:22026 | terms of the notification which the inspector thinks proper in the light
-- src:22027 | of the inspector’s investigation to be given by the Minister under
-- src:22028 | subsection (4).
@ref s 231(9) (src:22024-22028)
GIVEN `the Minister has directed that the report include a recommendation as to the terms of the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(9) the report must include a recommendation as to the terms of the notification` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has directed that the report include a recommendation as to the terms of the notification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the report "must, if the Minister so directs, include a recommendation"; an "if" unmet on a duty (fork F-K5)

@ref s 231(9) (src:22024-22028)
GIVEN `the inspector thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has directed that the report include a recommendation as to the terms of the notification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 231(9) the report may include a recommendation as to the terms of the notification` MEANS
    IF `the inspector thinks fit` OR `the Minister has directed that the report include a recommendation as to the terms of the notification`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the report "may if the inspector thinks fit, and must, if the Minister so directs"; a "may" with an "if" gate: the grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1 (fork F-K18)
